      "mechanism": "GHAST-based Transaction Ordering and Finality",
      "details": "Conflux's Tree-Graph consensus with the GHAST protocol processes blocks concurrently but enforces a deterministic total order of transactions. While this does not prevent contract-level reentrancy within a single transaction call trace, it eliminates transaction reordering and race-condition exploits (front-running/MEV-induced reentrancy vectors) typical in non-deterministic environments."
